WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.121 --> 00:00:04.639
(rock music)

00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:14.026
- I guess I haven't heard
really great things about it.

00:00:14.026 --> 00:00:15.802
- I assume it's all going to be nasty.

00:00:15.802 --> 00:00:18.057
- The other stuff I've
tried, I've kind of liked.

00:00:18.057 --> 00:00:19.083
I like fish and chips.

00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:21.003
- No one's like, "Oh, dude, we're getting

00:00:21.003 --> 00:00:22.709
"British food this week, yeah, we just

00:00:22.709 --> 00:00:23.963
"ordered some British food."

00:00:23.963 --> 00:00:25.190
- Well, the plates that I saw pass by

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:26.940
looked good, so hopefully.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.166
- I'm excited though.

00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:32.050
I'm down for the challenge.

00:00:34.781 --> 00:00:36.002
- Am I supposed to, like, dip it

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.987
in the sauce or something?

00:00:37.987 --> 00:00:40.263
- [Man] The gravy, they
took a hard-boiled egg

00:00:40.263 --> 00:00:41.958
and then just put meat around it.

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:45.905
- It's like Thanksgiving and
then just an egg in the middle.

00:00:45.905 --> 00:00:47.501
- Here we go.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:48.676
- I like that.

00:00:48.676 --> 00:00:51.026
- I don't.
- You don't like it?

00:00:51.026 --> 00:00:52.917
- I like how the spice is with the meat.

00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:55.292
- I like the stuffing,
I don't like the egg.

00:00:55.292 --> 00:00:56.702
- Honestly, it takes me back to

00:00:56.702 --> 00:00:58.281
a food that my grandfather made.

00:00:58.281 --> 00:01:00.155
- The meat reminds me of stuffing,

00:01:00.155 --> 00:01:02.292
so it's way too soft for me.

00:01:02.292 --> 00:01:04.788
- Britain has not really won me over yet.

00:01:04.788 --> 00:01:07.509
(rock music).

00:01:07.509 --> 00:01:10.836
- Welsh Rarebit, did I say it right?

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.949
- So much flavor in the cheese garnish.

00:01:12.949 --> 00:01:16.536
- I like the salty with
the crunchy, delicious.

00:01:16.536 --> 00:01:17.848
- I need to figure out where to get this.

00:01:17.848 --> 00:01:18.951
- I would have it again.

00:01:18.951 --> 00:01:21.389
It reminds me of an
up-scale grilled cheese.

00:01:21.389 --> 00:01:23.990
UK is still not winning, but
it's getting a little better.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:25.487
A lot better than the first one we had.

00:01:25.487 --> 00:01:28.506
(rock music)

00:01:28.506 --> 00:01:32.233
- Cornish Pasty, I thought
it looked like an empanada.

00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:33.393
- It looks like a croissant

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.494
stuffed with beef and vegetables.

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:37.433
- It reminds me of a pot pie.

00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:38.989
- I like this one, because it reminds me

00:01:38.989 --> 00:01:40.707
of a Jamaican beef patty.

00:01:40.707 --> 00:01:42.031
I could get down with this one.

00:01:42.031 --> 00:01:44.248
Cornwall, I think I'll have Cornwall.

00:01:44.248 --> 00:01:46.733
(rock music)

00:01:46.733 --> 00:01:50.030
- We have a steak,
mushroom and Guinness pie.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.432
- I love the chunks of meat
just swimming in gravy.

00:01:52.432 --> 00:01:54.975
- It smells really good, though.

00:01:54.975 --> 00:01:56.125
The meat's really good.

00:01:56.125 --> 00:01:58.000
- It kind of reminds me of an oxtail

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.372
from the Caribbean, but
obviously less spice.

00:02:01.372 --> 00:02:02.626
- I think it's pretty good.

00:02:02.626 --> 00:02:04.205
I'm getting pretty sold on this.

00:02:04.205 --> 00:02:05.888
- All of this is very filling.

00:02:05.888 --> 00:02:08.432
- It may not look like
American proportions,

00:02:08.432 --> 00:02:11.148
but I feel like the
food is just more dense.

00:02:11.148 --> 00:02:13.469
(rock music)

00:02:13.469 --> 00:02:15.988
- We've got the eccles cake
with currant and raisin.

00:02:15.988 --> 00:02:17.613
- I never liked raisins.

00:02:17.613 --> 00:02:18.403
- What about currants?

00:02:18.403 --> 00:02:19.623
- I don't know what those are.

00:02:19.623 --> 00:02:22.431
- You're not up on your "currant" affairs.

00:02:22.431 --> 00:02:26.031
Look at that!

00:02:26.031 --> 00:02:27.470
- I like this one.

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:29.548
- I like the big grain sugar on it.

00:02:29.548 --> 00:02:31.069
I feel like it adds a good texture

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:32.590
on top of the gooey inside.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.331
- The desserts are winning.

00:02:34.331 --> 00:02:37.460
This is where England did good.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:39.619
(rock music)

00:02:39.619 --> 00:02:42.924
So, we have some British scones.

00:02:42.924 --> 00:02:47.560
These ones are round shaped,
ours are usually triangular.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.417
The jam smells so good.

00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:52.018
The aroma (sniffs).

00:02:52.018 --> 00:02:56.696
- Is it like in poor taste
to dip your scone in the tea?

00:02:56.696 --> 00:02:57.450
- That's amazing.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.641
- This clotted cream is interesting.

00:02:58.641 --> 00:03:00.179
It's like butter, but more sour.

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:04.026
- British food is
definitely growing on me.

00:03:04.026 --> 00:03:06.418
- In the beginning, I thought
it was going to be horrible,

00:03:06.418 --> 00:03:09.321
awful, disgusting, but I will say

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:11.318
there are some things
that I've come to like.

00:03:11.318 --> 00:03:14.499
- I came into this pretty
skeptical of British food.

00:03:14.499 --> 00:03:15.857
I thought it might be gross.

00:03:15.857 --> 00:03:17.586
- I wouldn't ever say
it's really that bad.

00:03:17.586 --> 00:03:19.583
- I could definitely
see myself coming back

00:03:19.583 --> 00:03:22.521
and knowing some specific
things to try now,

00:03:22.521 --> 00:03:25.121
versus just having no idea.

00:03:25.121 --> 00:03:29.713
(rock music)

